Prerequisites
Node.js [20.x or 22.x LTS] — native modules (better-sqlite3, argon2) require an LTS build
npm [version]
Install & run
bash
git clone [your repo URL]
cd sprintpulse-lite
npm install

# copy and fill in environment variables
cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env
# open apps/api/.env and set JWT_SECRET to any random string of 32+ characters

npm run db:migrate
npm run db:seed
npm run dev

This starts three processes concurrently: the API, the background worker, and the Vite dev server.

Frontend: http://localhost:5173
API: http://localhost:[3000]
API docs (Swagger UI): http://localhost:[3000]/docs
Environment variables
Variable	Purpose	Required
PORT	API port	No, defaults to 3000
JWT_SECRET	Signs auth cookies, min 32 chars	Yes
DATABASE_URL	Path to the SQLite file	No, has a default
CORS_ORIGINS	Allowed frontend origin(s)	Yes for non-default setups
ADMIN_EMAILS	Comma-separated emails treated as admin	Optional
FAIL_RATE	0–1, artificially fails background jobs (for demoing retries)	No, defaults to 0
SMTP_*, MAIL_FROM, APP_URL	[If shipped] outbound email for invites/OTP	No — falls back to a console logger if unset
Running tests
bash
npm test
